# TrialBridge configuration
#
# Every variable here is OPTIONAL. The app runs with no configuration at all,
# and neither upstream service requires an API key.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` only if you need to override a default.
# NEVER commit `.env.local` — `.gitignore` already excludes it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private beta gate (HTTP Basic authentication)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set SITE_PASSWORD on your host to require a browser login before ANY page,
# asset, script bundle or API route can be loaded. Leave it unset for local
# development, or to reopen the site publicly (e.g. for challenge judges).
#
# Use a long random value. Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('base64url'))"
#
# Basic credentials are base64-encoded, not encrypted — only ever use this
# over HTTPS. Vercel and Replit both provide HTTPS automatically.
#
# SITE_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-long-random-string
# SITE_USERNAME=beta

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Geocoder endpoint
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Converts a city/state/country name into coordinates. Defaults to the public
# OpenStreetMap Nominatim service.
#
# The Nominatim Usage Policy requires that operators be able to switch away
# from the shared service "without requiring a software update", which is why
# this is an environment variable. Any Nominatim-compatible /search endpoint
# works — including a self-hosted instance, which is what you should use for
# anything beyond demo traffic.
#
# GEOCODER_URL=https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Geocoder User-Agent
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nominatim requires a User-Agent that identifies your application; stock
# HTTP-library User-Agents are explicitly rejected. Including a contact address
# is good practice so the OSMF can reach you instead of simply blocking you.
#
# Set this for any public deployment.
#
# GEOCODER_USER_AGENT=TrialBridge/1.0 (+https://your-domain.example; mailto:you@example.org)
